				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "TfNBa7Fdp83dOFhF6",
			"name": "Pathfinder Training",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Pathfinders are the Fire caste's scouts and forward observers: volunteers from the ranks who trade the line for an ahead-of-the-army life of stealth, long-range shooting and marking targets with markerlights for the guns behind them. Codex: T'au Empire background.\n\nDesign: Attribute Modifiers (Pathfinder) 30 + Steady Designator 1 = 31 points.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"T'au"
			],
			"container_type": "meta_trait",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "tarqOUOU7-bK95lc1",
					"name": "Attribute Modifiers (Pathfinder)",
					"local_notes": "DX +1, Per +2.\n\nDesign: Over the Fire Caste Lens: ST 10, DX 13, IQ 11, HT 11, HP 10, Per 13, Will 11, Move 6. DX +1 (20), Per +2 (10) = 30. Basic Speed (13+11)/4 = 6.0, Move 6.",
					"tags": [
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"T'au"
					],
					"base_points": 30,
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "dx",
							"amount": 1
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "per",
							"amount": 2
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "t4qtDIlR2SyiyB4Ef",
					"name": "Steady Designator",
					"reference": "B100",
					"local_notes": "+1 to Beam Weapons (Rifle) rolls made with a markerlight.\n\nLore: A Pathfinder's whole craft is holding a beam on a target long enough for the guns behind to lock.\n\nDesign: Perk (B100), 1 point: a narrow +1 limited to the designator.",
					"tags": [
						"Perk",
						"Xenos",
						"T'au"
					],
					"base_points": 1,
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "conditional_modifier",
							"situation": "to Beam Weapons (Rifle) rolls made to paint a target with a markerlight",
							"amount": 1
						}
					]
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "TSYK0DGsQRt7e9sJi",
			"name": "Battlesuit Pilot Training",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A Shas'vre is a veteran Fire Warrior who has been selected to wear a battlesuit: years of neural interface drill and marked physical and mental discipline. The stat line is the pilot's; the suit is equipment. Codex: T'au Empire background.\n\nDesign: Attribute Modifiers (Battlesuit Pilot) 85 + Suit Familiarity 1 = 86 points.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"T'au"
			],
			"container_type": "meta_trait",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "t8sZpzrifKMLHt0W1",
					"name": "Attribute Modifiers (Battlesuit Pilot)",
					"local_notes": "ST +1, DX +2, IQ +1, HT +1, Will +1.\n\nDesign: Over the Fire Caste Lens: ST 11, DX 14, IQ 12, HT 12, HP 11, Per 12, Will 13. ST +1 (10), DX +2 (40), IQ +1 (20), HT +1 (10), Will +1 (5) = 85. Basic Speed (14+12)/4 = 6.5, Move 6. Framework.md lists Move 5 for this line, which is not reachable honestly: a higher DX than the Shas'ui with the same HT cannot have lower Move without a paid Decreased Basic Move, and none is warranted. Move 6 it is.",
					"tags": [
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"T'au"
					],
					"base_points": 85,
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "st",
							"amount": 1
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "dx",
							"amount": 2
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "iq",
							"amount": 1
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "ht",
							"amount": 1
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "will",
							"amount": 1
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "tmSX6OMWXbi5P1bsA",
					"name": "Suit Familiarity",
					"reference": "B100",
					"local_notes": "No unfamiliarity penalty between T'au battlesuit patterns (Crisis, Stealth, Broadside).\n\nLore: T'au suits share a pilot interface; a veteran moves between patterns easily.\n\nDesign: Perk (B100), 1 point.",
					"tags": [
						"Perk",
						"Xenos",
						"T'au"
					],
					"base_points": 1
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "T98NSkKt1b3rPjlpy",
			"name": "Commander Lens (Shas'o)",
			"local_notes": "Kauyon and Mont'ka are the two T'au doctrines a Commander plans a campaign around. Both are house adaptations of the Codex's army rules to a personal scale: each perk is a plan the Commander must actually set up (a Tactics roll before the fight), and the bonus applies to allied ranged attacks in the Commander's network only at the times described.\n\nLore: A Shas'o is a Fire caste commander of decades' standing: a master of Kauyon, the Patient Hunter (lure, wait, and strike when the enemy has committed), and Mont'ka, the Killing Blow (strike fast and hard at a chosen moment). Codex: T'au Empire background for both doctrines.\n\nDesign: Attribute Modifiers (Commander) 145 + Kauyon 1 + Mont'ka 1 = 147 points; Military Rank 5 (25) is added separately in the template. Kauyon and Mont'ka are Perks (B100), not skills or techniques: a technique would cost more than the effect is worth, and Tactics already covers planning. The bonuses are conditional so they do not show as a stat.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Xenos",
				"T'au"
			],
			"container_type": "meta_trait",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "ti0QB3OubasNgBtdW",
					"name": "Attribute Modifiers (Commander)",
					"local_notes": "ST +1, DX +3, IQ +3, HT +1, Will +1.\n\nDesign: Over the Fire Caste Lens: ST 11, DX 15, IQ 14, HT 12, HP 11, Per 14, Will 15, Move 6. ST +1 (10), DX +3 (60), IQ +3 (60), HT +1 (10), Will +1 (5) = 145. Basic Speed (15+12)/4 = 6.75, Move 6, Per 14 = IQ 14.",
					"tags": [
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"T'au"
					],
					"base_points": 145,
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "st",
							"amount": 1
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "dx",
							"amount": 3
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "iq",
							"amount": 3
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "ht",
							"amount": 1
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "will",
							"amount": 1
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "tHQxakyV8B7W0nXA2",
					"name": "Kauyon (The Patient Hunter)",
					"reference": "B100",
					"local_notes": "+2 to Tactics to plan a Kauyon lure or ambush. On a success by 3+, T'au and auxiliary ranged attacks in the Commander's network get +1 to hit once the enemy has committed to the trap (GM's call, roughly the fourth turn on).\n\nLore: The Patient Hunter: hold back, bait the enemy in, and close the trap when it has committed.\n\nDesign: Perk (B100), 1 point: a narrow planning bonus. Chosen per engagement, not both.",
					"tags": [
						"Perk",
						"Xenos",
						"T'au"
					],
					"base_points": 1,
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "conditional_modifier",
							"situation": "to Tactics rolls to plan a lure, ambush or defence in depth",
							"amount": 2
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "txDwTQkLfW24BHEcx",
					"name": "Mont'ka (The Killing Blow)",
					"reference": "B100",
					"local_notes": "+2 to Tactics to plan a Mont'ka strike. On a success by 3+, T'au and auxiliary ranged attacks in the Commander's network get +1 to hit during the assault's first three turns.\n\nLore: The Killing Blow: strike fast and hard while the enemy is unprepared.\n\nDesign: Perk (B100), 1 point. Chosen per engagement, not both.",
					"tags": [
						"Perk",
						"Xenos",
						"T'au"
					],
					"base_points": 1,
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "conditional_modifier",
							"situation": "to Tactics rolls to plan a sudden strike at a chosen weak point",
							"amount": 2
						}
					]
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "TksAhUMaHXwFTpTQr",
			"name": "Ethereal Caste Lens",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Ethereals are the Empire's rulers: physically frail, mentally formidable, and treated by the other castes with something between reverence and worship. They seldom fight; their weapon is presence. Aun is the caste's name for itself (Aun'va was the Supreme Ruler). Codex: T'au Empire background.\n\nDesign: Attribute Modifiers (Ethereal) 85 + Status 5 (25) + Inspiring Presence 31 = 141 points. Status 5 because Ethereals sit at the top of a society ruled by them, as a monarch or a high priest would; a lower Status would understate how thoroughly the other castes defer.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Mental",
				"Xenos",
				"T'au"
			],
			"container_type": "meta_trait",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "tr43toIMj8XNyPcGY",
					"name": "Attribute Modifiers (Ethereal)",
					"local_notes": "ST -1, DX +1, IQ +3, Per -1, Will +4.\n\nDesign: Framework Aun line: ST 9, DX 11, IQ 13, HT 10, HP 9, Per 12, Will 17, Move 5. ST -1 (-10), DX +1 (20), IQ +3 (60), Per -1 (-5, so Per 12 with IQ 13), Will +4 (20, so Will 17 with IQ 13) = 85. Basic Speed (11+10)/4 = 5.25, Move 5, HP 9 = ST 9.",
					"tags": [
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"T'au"
					],
					"base_points": 85,
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "st",
							"amount": -1
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "dx",
							"amount": 1
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "iq",
							"amount": 3
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "per",
							"amount": -1
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "will",
							"amount": 4
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "twVoRtD0OLJB17QfG",
					"name": "Status (Ethereal Caste)",
					"reference": "B28",
					"local_notes": "Status 5: rulers and near-sacred figures to most T'au.\n\nLore: The Ethereals govern the Empire; the other castes serve.\n\nDesign: Status (B28, 5/level), 5 levels = 25 points.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Social",
						"Xenos",
						"T'au"
					],
					"points_per_level": 5,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 5
				},
				{
					"id": "TmkjGsnOndKrP-t25",
					"name": "Inspiring Presence",
					"local_notes": "The Ethereal's half of the Devotion pairing. T'au and T'au auxiliaries in sight or hearing of an Ethereal satisfy the Accessibility on Devotion to the Ethereals (Fearlessness +2, Higher Purpose +1) and react to the Ethereal at +4; non-T'au see only the Social Regard.\n\nLore: An Ethereal calms and steels the T'au around them: Fire Warriors under fire stay in place, and envoys see counsel followed. Many in the fiction suspect a pheromonal effect; it is never confirmed. Codex: T'au Empire background.\n\nDesign: Charisma 4 (B41, 5/level = 20) with Accessibility -20% (only T'au and their auxiliaries) = 16, plus Social Regard (Venerated) 3 (B87, 5/level) = 15: 31 points. Social Regard is separate because even foreign envoys treat an Ethereal with care; the Charisma is the aura proper. A true area buff was rejected as unbuildable from Basic Set traits without inventing new modifiers.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Social",
						"Xenos",
						"T'au"
					],
					"container_type": "meta_trait",
					"children": [
						{
							"id": "t5c8zwJ4_wyLJCA3N",
							"name": "Charisma (T'au and Auxiliaries)",
							"reference": "B41",
							"local_notes": "+4 to reactions and to Diplomacy, Leadership, Public Speaking, Politics and similar Influence rolls with T'au and their auxiliaries.\n\nLore: The Ethereal's pull on T'au society.\n\nDesign: Charisma 4 (B41, 5/level = 20), Accessibility -20% = 16 points.",
							"tags": [
								"Advantage",
								"Social",
								"Xenos",
								"T'au"
							],
							"modifiers": [
								{
									"id": "mBaj4H0K0uL-Ri64N",
									"name": "Accessibility",
									"reference": "B110",
									"local_notes": "Only affects T'au and T'au auxiliaries (Kroot, Vespid, Gue'vesa), not other species.",
									"cost_adj": "-20%"
								}
							],
							"points_per_level": 5,
							"can_level": true,
							"levels": 4
						},
						{
							"id": "tvfhP6i9pSGbtCoU0",
							"name": "Social Regard (Venerated Ethereal)",
							"reference": "B87",
							"local_notes": "Venerated: +3 reactions from those who hold Ethereals in awe.\n\nLore: To most T'au, and to many others, an Ethereal is very nearly sacred.\n\nDesign: Social Regard (Venerated) 3 (B87, 5/level) = 15 points.",
							"tags": [
								"Advantage",
								"Social",
								"Xenos",
								"T'au"
							],
							"points_per_level": 5,
							"can_level": true,
							"levels": 3
						}
					]
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "TxUAA8Hh0sTYyNEr6",
			"name": "Earth Caste Lens",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Earth caste are the Empire's engineers, builders and technologists: shorter, broader and stockier than the other castes, patient and practical. Their work built the Empire's drones, suits and vehicles. Codex: T'au Empire background.\n\nDesign: Attribute Modifiers (Earth Caste) 95 + Fit 5 = 100 points.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
