				{
					"id": "tAG29SHAN1JWKoBdm",
					"name": "Fit",
					"reference": "B55",
					"local_notes": "+1 to HT rolls to stay conscious or avoid dying; recovers lost FP faster (B55).\n\nLore: Fire caste and Earth caste both spend their lives on their feet and in kit.\n\nDesign: Fit (B55), 5 points.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"T'au"
					],
					"base_points": 5
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "TfR8bBtil2cB6rEAt",
			"name": "Water Caste Lens",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Water caste are the Empire's diplomats, merchants and administrators: the caste that carries the Greater Good to other worlds and other species. They are lightly built, persuasive and practised at reading and adapting to strangers. Codex: T'au Empire background.\n\nDesign: Attribute Modifiers (Water Caste) 45 + Cultural Adaptability 10 + Language Talent 10 = 65 points. 'Tongue as weapon' is these two traits and the Diplomacy-heavy skill list, not a Charisma purchase.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Social",
				"Xenos",
				"T'au"
			],
			"container_type": "meta_trait",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "tenS1Q_AsDUhf9Lq7",
					"name": "Attribute Modifiers (Water Caste)",
					"local_notes": "ST -1, IQ +3, Per -1.\n\nDesign: Framework Por line: ST 9, DX 10, IQ 13, HT 10, HP 9, Per 12, Will 13, Move 5. ST -1 (-10), IQ +3 (60), Per -1 (-5) = 45. Will 13 = IQ 13 with no separate bonus. Basic Speed (10+10)/4 = 5.0, Move 5, HP 9 = ST 9.",
					"tags": [
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"T'au"
					],
					"base_points": 45,
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "st",
							"amount": -1
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "iq",
							"amount": 3
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "per",
							"amount": -1
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "t-tZKzR61jH9xEWou",
					"name": "Cultural Adaptability",
					"reference": "B46",
					"local_notes": "No unfamiliarity penalty in any culture; the Water caste's trade.\n\nLore: Water caste envoys are trained to be at home wherever they are sent.\n\nDesign: Cultural Adaptability (B46), 10 points.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Social",
						"Xenos",
						"T'au"
					],
					"base_points": 10
				},
				{
					"id": "t57bhSAvIeI563NRX",
					"name": "Language Talent",
					"reference": "B65",
					"local_notes": "+2 to learning and using languages (B65).\n\nLore: T'au diplomacy runs on speaking the other side's tongue.\n\nDesign: Language Talent (B65), 10 points.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Mental",
						"Xenos",
						"T'au"
					],
					"base_points": 10
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "T52cKl8mAcYrlkcY6",
			"name": "Air Caste Lens",
			"local_notes": "Lore: Air caste are the Empire's pilots, navigators and couriers: tall, slender and light-boned, adapted to life aloft and in low gravity, and at ease in a cockpit or free fall in a way other castes are not. They bear high gravity badly. Codex: T'au Empire background.\n\nDesign: Attribute Modifiers (Air Caste) 75 + Skinny -5 + G-Experience 2 - G-Intolerance 10 = 62 points. Hollow bones are built as Skinny plus ST 8 / HP 8; the Basic Set has no 'hollow bones' trait and Fragile (Brittle) at -15 would be too harsh for a species that does not shatter. G-Intolerance uses B137's 0.1G-increment tier; the drafter could not reproduce the exact B137 text from memory, so the GM should apply B137's own rule for the penalty size.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"T'au"
			],
			"container_type": "meta_trait",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "tg7sL41JZTY2ktVLi",
					"name": "Attribute Modifiers (Air Caste)",
					"local_notes": "ST -2, DX +3, IQ +2, Will -1.\n\nDesign: Framework Kor line: ST 8, DX 13, IQ 12, HT 10, HP 8, Per 12, Will 11, Move 5. ST -2 (-20), DX +3 (60), IQ +2 (40), Will -1 (-5) = 75. Basic Speed (13+10)/4 = 5.75, Move 5, HP 8 = ST 8.",
					"tags": [
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"T'au"
					],
					"base_points": 75,
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "st",
							"amount": -2
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "dx",
							"amount": 3
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "iq",
							"amount": 2
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "will",
							"amount": -1
						}
					]
				},
				{
					"id": "t7uR4brCwnY1x1VA0",
					"name": "Skinny (Slender Frame)",
					"reference": "B18",
					"local_notes": "Tall, light-boned and narrow: -2 to Disguise and Shadowing, -2 ST against knockback (B18).\n\nLore: Air caste are noticeably tall and slight.\n\nDesign: Skinny (B18), -5 points.",
					"tags": [
						"Disadvantage",
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"T'au"
					],
					"base_points": -5
				},
				{
					"id": "tKBNUNFqKJDnlExEn",
					"name": "G-Experience (Zero-G and Low Gravity)",
					"reference": "B57",
					"local_notes": "No skill penalties in zero gravity or in low gravity.\n\nLore: Air caste train and live in low-gravity habitats and free fall.\n\nDesign: G-Experience (B57), 1 point per gravity band, 2 bands (zero-G, low-G) = 2 points.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"T'au"
					],
					"points_per_level": 1,
					"can_level": true,
					"levels": 2
				},
				{
					"id": "tzKYgHezrsucOjR0F",
					"name": "G-Intolerance (High Gravity)",
					"reference": "B137",
					"local_notes": "Suffers in gravity above Earth-normal; apply B137's rules for the penalty size.\n\nLore: Air caste bodies are poorly suited to high gravity and heavy loads.\n\nDesign: G-Intolerance (0.1G increment) (B137), -10 points.",
					"tags": [
						"Disadvantage",
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"T'au"
					],
					"base_points": -10
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "T0ovKmzn3LJvvn9NP",
			"name": "Kroot Physiology",
			"local_notes": "Lore: The Kroot are lean, avian-looking carnivores: hunched, long-limbed, beaked and quilled. They fight for the Empire as mercenaries, live in nomadic kindreds led by Shapers, and are best known for genetic absorption: by eating what they kill they slowly take on its traits over generations. Codex: T'au Empire background, Kroot Mercenaries.\n\nDesign: Attribute Modifiers (Kroot) 105 + Sharp Beak 1 + Acute Taste & Smell 2 (4) + Born Climber 1 + Born Tracker 1 + Genetic Absorption 0 = 112 points, giving framework.md's Kroot Carnivore line before training. Not priced: Low TL (Kroot culture is primitive but Kroot use T'au and their own guns competently; the drafter is not confident enough to charge -5), Carnivore diet (no ancestry trait; handled in the Kindred trait as a habit).",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"T'au",
				"Kroot"
			],
			"container_type": "ancestry",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "t_4NsWiMSkl5vKlkB",
					"name": "Attribute Modifiers (Kroot)",
					"local_notes": "ST +2, DX +3, IQ -1, HT +1, Per +4, Will +1, Basic Move +2.\n\nDesign: Framework Kroot Carnivore line: ST 12, DX 13, IQ 9, HT 11, HP 12, Per 13, Will 10, Move 8. ST +2 (20), DX +3 (60), IQ -1 (-20), HT +1 (10), Per +4 (20, so Per 13 with IQ 9), Will +1 (5), Basic Move +2 (B17, 5/level = 10) = 105. Basic Speed (13+11)/4 = 6.0, Move 6 + 2 = 8, HP 12 = ST 12.",
					"tags": [
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"T'au",
						"Kroot"
					],
					"base_points": 105,
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "st",
							"amount": 2
						},
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
