				},
				{
					"id": "tD_rYgOGYYhHw5dbL",
					"name": "Flight (Grav Repulsors)",
					"reference": "B56",
					"local_notes": "Air Move is Basic Speed x 2: 10 for a gun drone. Hovers; superscience (^) grav repulsors.\n\nLore: T'au drones hover on grav repulsors; the framework marks grav systems as the T'au's one superscience exception.\n\nDesign: Flight (B56), 40 points, no Winged limitation (grav, not wings). Marked ^ by the framework rule for T'au grav technology.",
					"tags": [
						"Advantage",
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"T'au",
						"Drone"
					],
					"base_points": 40
				},
				{
					"id": "tqhZ6b8DSrx2KS4ZH",
					"name": "No Legs (Aerial)",
					"reference": "B145",
					"local_notes": "No legs; it flies. Ground Move does not apply.\n\nLore: A drone is a hovering shell.\n\nDesign: No Legs (Aerial) (B145), 0 points.",
					"tags": [
						"Feature",
						"Xenos",
						"T'au",
						"Drone"
					],
					"base_points": 0
				},
				{
					"id": "tIoHNhU1sdz-xXtcd",
					"name": "No Manipulators",
					"reference": "B145",
					"local_notes": "Cannot manipulate objects; guns are built in. ST and DX cost 40% less (B145).\n\nLore: A gun drone has weapons but no hands.\n\nDesign: No Manipulators (B145), -50 points; the ST cost reduction is applied in Attribute Modifiers (Drone).",
					"tags": [
						"Disadvantage",
						"Physical",
						"Xenos",
						"T'au",
						"Drone"
					],
					"base_points": -50
				},
				{
					"id": "T7I3mvTSjF_gxRTIN",
					"name": "Machine Mind (Drone AI)",
					"local_notes": "Takes orders, does nothing on its own initiative, cannot improvise, feels nothing. Follows its controller (a Shas'ui or pilot, or the fire team's network); another controller can be slotted in.\n\nLore: Drones are simple learning AIs: obedient, unimaginative, and without emotions the T'au recognise as their own. Codex: T'au Empire background.\n\nDesign: Slave Mentality -40 + Hidebound -5 + Incurious -5 + Low Empathy -20 + No Sense of Humor -10 + Reprogrammable -10 = -90. Slave Mentality replaces the Automaton's Heteronomy (same cost, B154); Incurious is priced at the library's -5 base rather than -10.",
					"tags": [
						"Disadvantage",
						"Mental",
						"Xenos",
						"T'au",
						"Drone"
					],
					"container_type": "meta_trait",
					"children": [
						{
							"id": "tRdiZevRU44Gko7h1",
							"name": "Slave Mentality",
							"reference": "B154",
							"local_notes": "Cannot act without orders; obeys its controller.\n\nLore: Drones do what they are told.\n\nDesign: Slave Mentality (B154), -40 points.",
							"tags": [
								"Disadvantage",
								"Mental",
								"Xenos",
								"T'au",
								"Drone"
							],
							"base_points": -40
						},
